;; repr/ocaml's read level's divergences (bin/reap's OCaml read cell; doc/ocaml/OCAML-SURVEY.md, "As built: O8 (write-ahead)"):
;; the classes every file of test/ocaml/read-results.edn that does not pass falls into, in test/goi/divergences.edn's format,
;; matched against "RESULT REASON" as the record writes them (REASON "CLASS KIND: MESSAGE", the class bin/repr-ocaml roundtrip
;; gives a file the parser rejects, test/ocaml/roundtrip-known.edn's). Since 2026-11-16 the record is the native reader's
;; (arbace.repr.ocaml.native: OCaml 5.5.0's lexer.mll and parser.mly ported; before, the oracle's, tools/ocdump on compiler-libs,
;; whose rows the native record repeats row for row): a file it rejects is the corpus's, judged on the parser's message (survey
;; §5.4), not a read failure of Arbace's.
;; Read with the Clojure reader.
[
 {:id :oracle-rejects
  :title "files OCaml's parser rejects that no test of theirs reads: the opam set's build scripts, toplevel init files and preprocessor input"
  :kind :design
  :why "since OC213 (a) (the user, 2026-11-10) the testsuite's files the reader rejects are judged by their own tests (bin/repr-ocaml own-read: ocamlc.byte's .compilers.reference, the expect tool's and the toplevel's reads) and all 61 pass, so the class holds the opam set's 17: their pkg/pkg.ml, build.ml and toplevel init files use topfind directives, yojson's files cppo's: none is OCaml ocamlc accepts. The read level reads what OCaml's parser reads; each rejection is recorded with the parser's message (roundtrip-known.edn), which the round trip checks unchanged (the native reader's since 2026-11-16)"
  :decided "survey §5.4; O2, O7 (\"As built\": the helper's rejections classed); OC213 (a), 2026-11-10 (the testsuite's own verdicts)"
  :match [#"^reject (syntax-error|lexer-error) (syntax|lexer): "]}
 {:id :templates
  :title "the stdlib's macro templates"
  :kind :design
  :why "stdlib/templates/*.template.mli are inputs to the stdlib's build (sed templates for Float and MoreLabels), not OCaml"
  :decided "O1 (test/ocaml/corpora.edn's :ocdump-rejects)"
  :match [#"^reject template syntax: "]}]
